                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_106">Cambridge, Cambridgeshire.
                        Peterhouse (Collegium Sancti Petri)</orgName><p>Notes in the hand of
                           <persName role="fmo">William Dyngley</persName>, fol. 1r. </p><p><q>On
                           the verso of the last stub can be read <q>[...]ebrig'</q>, s. xiv,
                           doubtless the end of a Peterhouse ex libris.</q> (Thomson,
                           <title>Peterhouse</title>, 69).</p><p> In the Peterhouse catalogue of
                        1418.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_247">Hereford,
                        Herefordshire, Cathedral church of St Ethelbert</orgName>
                     <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of
                        Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the Supplement (1987). The
                        corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain index card covers both MSS
                        112 and 119. It originally recorded the following evidence:</p>
                     <p>Contains copy of a letter from R. precentor Hereford to Stephen Abbot of
                        Dore, also a pencil inscription containing the words <q>thoma vicar de
                           Wenford herefordens, nomine pensionis</q>.</p><p>The following
                        two notes were later added on the card:</p><p>
                        <q>No Winford in Hereford diocese - Winforton and Wentnor, both
                           rectories</q>; <q>Dore seems equally likely.
                     Rejected.</q></p></provenance>
